G1411.b:
⟪δύναμις⟫, -εως, ἡ
(< δύναμαι), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨חַיִל⁩ (⁨חֵיל⁩) , ⁨ץָבָא⁩, ⁨גְּבוּרָה⁩, ⁨עֹו⁩, etc.; 35 words in all;] ⟪power, might, strength⟫; relatively, ⟪ability, power⟫ to perform: ⟦Matthew 25:15|Mt 25:15⟧, ⟦Acts 3:2|Ac 3:2⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:11|He 11:11⟧; κατὰ δ., ⟦2 Corinthians 8:3|II Co 8:3⟧; παρὰ δ., ⟦2 Corinthians 8:3|ib.⟧ ; ὑπὲρ δ., ⟦2 Corinthians 1:8|II Co 1:8⟧; of pecuniary ability, ⟦2 Corinthians 8:3|II Co 8:3⟧, ⟦Revelation 18:3|Re 18:3⟧; absol., ⟪power, might⟫: ⟦Luke 24:49|Lk 24:49⟧, ⟦Acts 1:8|Ac 1:8⟧; opp. to ἀσθένεια, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:43|I Co 15:43⟧ ; ἡ δ. τ. ἁμαρτίας, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:56|I Co 15:56⟧; of power in action, ⟦Romans 1:16|Ro 1:16⟧, ⟦Romans 1:20|20⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:18|I Co l:18⟧, ⟦Philippians 3:10|Phl 3:10⟧, al. ἡ δ. τ. Θεοῦ, ⟦Matthew 22:29|Mt 22:29⟧, ⟦Mark 12:24|Mk 12:24⟧, ⟦Romans 1:20|Ro 1:20⟧, al.; opp. to μόρφωσις, ⟦2 Timothy 3:5|II Ti 3:5⟧; in doxologies, ⟦Revelation 4:11|Re 4:11⟧ ⟦Revelation 7:12|7:12⟧, al. ; ἐν δ., ⟦Mark 9:1|Mk 9:1⟧, ⟦Luke 4:36|Lk 4:36⟧, ⟦Romans 1:4|Ro 1:4⟧, al. ; of the power of performing miracles, ⟦Acts 6:8|Ac 6:8⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:9|II Th 2:9⟧ ; pl., ⟦Matthew 13:54|Mt 13:54⟧, ⟦Mark 6:14|Mk 6:14⟧, ⟦Galatians 3:5|Ga 3:5⟧, al. ; of the ⟪force⟫ or ⟪meaning⟫ of a word (Plat., al.), ⟦1 Corinthians 14:11|I Co 14:11⟧. By meton., of persons or things;
⟪(a)⟫ of God, ⟦Matthew 26:64|Mt 26:64⟧, ⟦Mark 14:62|Mk 14:62⟧ (Dalman, Words, 200 ff.) ;
⟪(b)⟫ of angels, ⟦Romans 8:38|Ro 8:38⟧, ⟦Ephesians 1:21|Eph 1:21⟧, ⟦1 Peter 3:22|I Pe 3:22⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ of armies, pl. [LXX for ⁨צְבָאוֺת⁩], metaph., of the stars, ⟦Matthew 24:29|Mt 24:29⟧, ⟦Mark 13:25|Mk 13:25⟧, ⟦Luke 21:26|Lk 21:26⟧;
⟪(d)⟫ of that wh. manifests God's power : Christ, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:24|I Co 1:24⟧; τ. εὐαγγέλιον, ⟦Romans 1:16|Ro 1:16⟧; ἡ δ. τ. κυρίου, ⟦1 Corinthians 5:4|I Co 5:4⟧;
⟪(e)⟫ of mighty works (Tr., Syn., § xci), δ. ποιεῖν, ⟦Mark 6:5|Mk 6:5⟧ ⟦Mark 9:39|9:39⟧; pl., ⟦Matthew 7:22|Mt 7:22⟧, ⟦Mark 6:2|Mk 6:2⟧, ⟦Luke 10:13|Lk 10:13⟧, al.; σημεῖα κ. δ.,. ⟦Acts 8:13|Ac 8:13⟧ ; δ. κ. τέρατα κ. σημεῖα, ⟦Acts 2:22|Ac 2:22⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 12:12|II Co 12:12⟧.
SYN.: βία, ἐνέργεια, ἐξουσία, ἰσχύς, κράτος (v. Tr., l.c.; Cremer, 218, 236; DB, i, 616; iv, 29; DCG, i, 607; ii, 188).

G1437.b:
⟪ἐάν⟫, contr. fr. εἰ ἄν, conditional particle, representing something as "under certain circumstances actual or liable to happen," but not so definitely expected as in the case of εἰ c. ind. (Bl., §65, 4; cf. ⟦John 13:17|Jo 13:17⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:36|I Co 7:36⟧), ⟪if haply, if⟫;
⟪1.⟫ c. subjc. (cl.);
	⟪(a)⟫ pres.: ⟦Matthew 6:22|Mt 6:22⟧, ⟦Luke 10:6|Lk 10:6⟧, ⟦John 7:17|Jo 7:17⟧, ⟦Romans 2:25|Ro 2:25⟧, ⟦Romans 2:26|26⟧ al.;
	⟪(b)⟫ aor. (= Lat. fut. pf.): ⟦Matthew 4:9|Mt 4:9⟧ ⟦Matthew 16:26|16:26⟧ (cf. ptcp. in ⟦Luke 9:25|Lk 9:25⟧; M, Pr., 230), ⟦Mark 3:24|Mk 3:24⟧, ⟦Luke 14:34|Lk 14:34⟧, ⟦John 5:43|Jo 5:43⟧, ⟦Romans 7:2|Ro 7:2⟧, al.; = cl. εἰ, c. opt., ⟦John 9:22|Jo 9:22⟧ ⟦John 11:57|11:57⟧, ⟦Acts 9:2|Ac 9:2⟧; as Heb. ⁨אִם⁩ = ὅταν, ⟦John 12:32|Jo 12:32⟧ ⟦John 14:3|14:3⟧, ⟦1 John 2:28|I Jo 2:28⟧ ⟦1 John 3:2|3:2⟧, ⟦Hebrews 3:7|He 3:7⟧ (LXX).
⟪2.⟫ C. indic, (as in late writers, fr. Arist. on; v. WH, App., 171; VD, MGr. 2, App., §77; Deiss., BS, 201f., LAE, 155, 254; M, Pr., 168, 187; Bl., §65, 4);
	⟪(a)⟫ fut.: ⟦Matthew 18:19|Mt 18:19⟧ T, ⟦Luke 19:40|Lk 19:40⟧, ⟦Acts 7:7|Ac 7:7⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ pres.: ⟦1 Thessalonians 3:8|I Th 3:8⟧ (v. Milligan, in l.).
⟪3.⟫ With other particles: ἐ. καί (Bl., §65, 6), ⟦Galatians 6:1|Ga 6:1⟧; ἐ. μή (M, Pr., 185, 187; Bl., l.c.), c. subjc. pres., ⟦Matthew 10:13|Mt 10:13⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 8:8|I Co 8:8⟧, ⟦James 2:17|Ja 2:17⟧, ⟦1 John 3:21|I Jo 3:21⟧; aor., ⟦Matthew 6:15|Mt 6:15⟧, ⟦Mark 3:27|Mk 3:27⟧, ⟦John 3:3|Jo 3:3⟧, ⟦Romans 10:15|Ro 10:15⟧, ⟦Galatians 1:8|Ga 1:8⟧ ⟦Galatians 2:16|2:16⟧ (v. Lft., Ellic., in ll.); ἐ. τε . . . ἐ. τε, [in LXX for ⁨אִם . . . אִם⁩, ⟦Esther 19:13|Es 19:13⟧, al.,] ⟦Romans 14:8|Ro 14:8⟧.
⟪4.⟫ = cl. ἄν (q.v.) after relat. pronouns and adverbs (Tdf., Pr., 96; WH, App., 173; M, Pr., 42f.; Bl., §26, 4; Mayser, 152f.; Deiss., BS, 202ff.): ὃς ἐ., ⟦Matthew 5:19|Mt 5:19⟧, ⟦Mark 6:22|Mk 6:22⟧, ⟦Mark 6:23|23⟧ ⟦Luke 17:32|Lk 17:32⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 6:18|I Co 6:18⟧, al.; ὅπου ἐ., ⟦Matthew 8:19|Mt 8:19⟧; ὁσάκις ἐ., ⟦Revelation 11:6|Re 11:6⟧; οὗ ἐ., ⟦1 Corinthians 16:6|I Co 16:6⟧; καθὸ ἐ., ⟦2 Corinthians 8:12|II Co 8:12⟧; ὅστις ἐ., ⟦Galatians 5:10|Ga 5:10⟧.

G1488.b:
⟪εἰμί⟫, with various uses and significations, like the English verb ⟪to be⟫.
⟪I.⟫ As substantive verb.
	⟪1.⟫ Of persons and things, ⟪to be, exist⟫: ⟦Acts 17:28|Ac 17:28⟧, ⟦John 1:1|Jo 1:1⟧ ⟦John 8:58|8:58⟧ ⟦John 17:5|17:5⟧, al; ὁ ὢν καὶ ὁ ἦν (for past ptcp.), ⟦Revelation 1:4|Re 1:4⟧, ⟦Revelation 1:8|8⟧ ⟦Revelation 4:8|4:8⟧ ⟦Revelation 11:17|11:17⟧ ⟦Revelation 16:5|16:5⟧ (v. Swete, Ap., 5; M, Pr., 228); τὰ (μὴ) ὄντα, ⟦Romans 4:17|Ro 4:17⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:28|I Co 1:28⟧.
	⟪2.⟫ Of times, events, etc., ⟪to be, happen, take place⟫: ⟦Matthew 24:3|Mt 24:3⟧, ⟦Mark 14:2|Mk 14:2⟧ ⟦Mark 15:42|15:42⟧, ⟦Luke 21:23|Lk 21:23⟧, ⟦John 4:6|Jo 4:6⟧, ⟦John 4:23|23⟧ ⟦John 5:10|5:10⟧, al.
	⟪3.⟫ ⟪to be present, be⟫ in a place, ⟪have come⟫: ⟦Matthew 2:13|Mt 2:13⟧, ⟦Matthew 2:15|15⟧, ⟦Mark 1:45|Mk 1:45⟧ ⟦Mark 5:21|5:21⟧ ⟦Mark 15:40|15:40⟧, ⟦Luke 1:80|Lk 1:80⟧ ⟦Luke 5:29|5:29⟧, ⟦John 7:30|Jo 7:30⟧, al.; seq. εἰς, ⟦Mark 2:1|Mk 2:1⟧; seq. ἐκ, (ἐξ), ⟦Matthew 1:20|Mt 1:20⟧ ⟦Matthew 21:25|21:25⟧, ⟦Mark 11:30|Mk 11:30⟧, ⟦John 3:31|Jo 3:31⟧, al.
	⟪4.⟫ Impers., ἔστι, ἦν, etc.;
		⟪(a)⟫ ⟪there is⟫ (Fr. il y a), ⟪was⟫, etc.: ⟦Matthew 16:28|Mt 16:28⟧, ⟦Luke 16:19|Lk 16:19⟧, ⟦John 3:1|Jo 3:1⟧ ⟦John 5:2|5:2⟧, ⟦Romans 3:10|Ro 3:10⟧, al.; c. dat. (of the possessor; Bl., §37, 3), ⟦Matthew 16:22|Mt 16:22⟧, ⟦Luke 1:7|Lk 1:7⟧, ⟦John 18:10|Jo 18.10⟧, ⟦Romans 9:2|Ro 9:2⟧, al.; ἔστιν ὅς, ὅστις (chiefly in pl), ⟦Matthew 16:28|Mt 16:28⟧ ⟦Matthew 19:2|19:2⟧, ⟦Mark 9:1|Mk 9:1⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ c. inf., = ἔξεστιν (q.v.), ⟪it is possible⟫: ⟦Hebrews 9:5|He 9:5⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 11:20|I Co 11:20⟧, RV (but v. ICC, in l.).
⟪II.⟫ As copula uniting subject and predicate.
	⟪1.⟫ Expressing simply identity or equivalence: ⟦Matthew 5:13|Mt 5:13⟧ ⟦Matthew 14:15|14:15⟧, ⟦Luke 1:18|Lk 1:18⟧, ⟦Luke 1:19|19⟧, ⟦John 1:1|Jo 1:1⟧ ⟦John 4:19|4:19⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:9|Re 3:9⟧, al. mult.
	⟪2.⟫ Explicative, as in parable, figure, type, etc.: ⟦Matthew 13:19|Mt 13:19⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 9:2|I Co 9:2⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 10:4|10:4⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 11:25|11:25⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:24|Ga 4:24⟧, ⟦Revelation 17:15|Re 17:15⟧, al.; τοῦτ’ ἔστιν, ⟦Matthew 27:46|Mt 27:46⟧, ⟦Mark 7:2|Mk 7:2⟧, ⟦Romans 7:18|Ro 7:18⟧ al.; ὅ ἐστιν, ⟦Mark 3:17|Mk 3:17⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:24|Col 1:24⟧, ⟦Hebrews 7:2|He 7:2⟧, al.; akin to this is the sacramental usage: ⟦Matthew 26:26|Mt 26:26-28⟧, ⟦Mark 14:22|Mk 14:22⟧, ⟦Mark 14:24|24⟧, ⟦Luke 22:19|Lk 22:19⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 11:24|I Co 11:24⟧ (v. ICC on Mk, I Co, ll. c.; DB, iii, 148 f.).
	⟪3.⟫ C. gen.: qual., etc., ⟦Mark 5:42|Mk 5:42⟧, ⟦Luke 3:23|Lk 3:23⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:33|I Co 14:33⟧, ⟦Hebrews 12:11|He 12:11⟧, al.; part., ⟦1 Timothy 1:20|I Ti 1:20⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 1:15|II Ti 1:15⟧; poss., ⟦Matthew 5:3|Mt 5:3⟧, ⟦Matthew 5:10|10⟧, ⟦Mark 12:7|Mk 12:7⟧, ⟦Luke 4:7|Lk 4:7⟧; of service or partisanship, ⟦Romans 8:9|Ro 8:9⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:12|I Co 1:12⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 10:7|II Co 10:7⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 2:19|II Ti 2:19⟧.
	⟪4.⟫ C. dat. (BL, §37, 3): ⟦Acts 1:8|Ac 1:8⟧ ⟦Acts 9:15|9:15⟧, ⟦Romans 4:12|Ro 4:12⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:18|I Co 1:18⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 2:14|2:14⟧, ⟦Revelation 21:7|Re 21:7⟧, al.
	⟪5.⟫ C. ptcp., as a periphrasis for the simple verb (Bl., §62, 1, 2; M, Pr., 225 ff.);
		⟪(a)⟫ c. ptcp. pf. (cl.): ⟦Matthew 10:30|Mt 10:30⟧, ⟦Luke 9:32|Lk 9:32⟧, ⟦John 3:24|Jo 3:24⟧, ⟦Acts 21:35|Ac 21:35⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:19|I Co 15:19⟧, al;
		⟪(b)⟫ c. ptcp. pr. (esp. in impf., as in Heb. and Aram.; Dalman, Words, 35 f.), ⟦Matthew 7:29|Mt 7:29⟧, ⟦Mark 1:22|Mk 1:22⟧, ⟦Luke 4:31|Lk 4:31⟧ ⟦Luke 14:1|14:1⟧, ⟦Acts 1:10|Ac 1:10⟧, al. mult., id. for imper. (M, Pr., 180f., 182f.), with ellipsis of εἰμί, ⟦Romans 12:9|Ro 12:9⟧, ⟦Romans 12:10|10⟧, ⟦Hebrews 13:5|He 13:5⟧, al.;
		⟪(c)⟫ c. ptcp. aor. (cl), ⟦Luke 23:9|Lk 23:9⟧.
	⟪6.⟫ Seq. εἰς (cf. Heb. ⁨הָיָה לְ⁩), a vernac. usage (M, Pr., 71): ⟦Matthew 19:5|Mt 19:5⟧, ⟦Mark 10:8|Mk 10:8⟧, ⟦Hebrews 8:10|He 8:10⟧, al.
	⟪7.⟫ C. adv.: ⟦Matthew 19:20|Mt 19:20⟧, ⟦Mark 4:26|Mk 4:26⟧, ⟦Luke 18:11|Lk 18:11⟧, al.
	⟪8.⟫ Ellipses;
		⟪(a)⟫ of the copula (Bl., §30, 3): ⟦Matthew 8:29|Mt 8:29⟧ ⟦Matthew 24:32|24:32⟧, ⟦John 21:22|Jo 21:22⟧, ⟦John 21:23|23⟧, ⟦Hebrews 6:4|He 6:4⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ of the predicate: ἐγώ εἰμί, ⟦Matthew 14:27|Mt 14:27⟧, ⟦Mark 6:50|Mk 6:50⟧, al.; absol. (cf. ⟦Deuteronomy 32:39|De 32:39⟧; ⁨אֲנִי הוּא⁩), ⟦Mark 13:6|Mk 13:6⟧, ⟦John 4:26|Jo 4:26⟧, al. (cf. ἄπ-, ἔν-, πάρ-, συμ-πάρ-, σύν-ειμι).

